# Ignore rules for a repo using this dev system.
# Marker convention (see templates/README.md for the full explanation):
#   "synced" blocks are owned by dev-system and overwritten by `callum-dev update`.
#   "repo-owned" blocks are yours - `callum-dev update` merges around them and never clobbers them.
#
# Note the block order here is the reverse of the other templates, deliberately:
# gitignore precedence is last-match-wins, so the repo-owned block sits at the
# BOTTOM. That is what lets a repo override or un-ignore a synced default with a
# `!` negation. Putting it first would leave repo rules silently outranked.

# --- synced: do not edit (managed by dev-system) ---

# This system's own tooling.

# no-mistakes pipeline state: its internal per-run worktrees, step logs and evidence.
# Directory-only pattern on purpose - see the must-not-ignore note below.
.no-mistakes/

# treehouse worktrees. treehouse.toml ships `root = "./"`, which places them at
# .treehouse/ inside the repo - each one a full working copy of this repo.
.treehouse/
.claude/worktrees/

# Claude Code's per-user local overrides. The shared .claude/settings.json is
# committed (dev-system syncs it); this file is machine-local and must not be.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Deliberately NOT ignored - these are committed on purpose, so do not "tidy them
# up" into the list above:
#   .callum-dev.json        the applied template version stamp
#   .callum-dev/baseline/   pristine template copies
#     Both are what make `callum-dev update` a real 3-way merge rather than an
#     overwrite. Ignoring them breaks updates for every fresh clone (README.md).
#   .no-mistakes.yaml       this repo's pipeline config, which lives right next to
#     the ignored .no-mistakes/ state directory. This is why the rule above ends
#     in a slash: a bare `.no-mistakes` would be one typo from catching the config.

# Node / TypeScript.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Playwright.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/

# Python.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
coverage/
htmlcov/

# Secrets and credentials. Keep an `.env.example` tracked as the documented shape.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
id_ed25519*
id_rsa*

# Logs.
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# OS and editor cruft. `.vscode/` is deliberately absent - projects using this
# system ship devcontainers and often commit shared editor settings on purpose.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/

# --- end synced ---

# --- repo-owned: edit freely ---
# This repo's own paths: build output under a non-standard name, local databases,
# fixture data, generated clients, vendored dependencies. Anything specific to
# this project rather than to the dev system belongs here, not above.
#
# Last-match-wins applies, so this is also where to un-ignore something a synced
# rule catches, e.g.:
#   !docs/design/**/*.png
# --- end repo-owned ---
